  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "While refining earth treasury flower Gu, Fang Yuan uses eight desolate blood powder: blood of eight kinds of immemorial desolate beasts, mixed, solidified, and ground into powder.",
      "chapters": [
        378
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_earth_treasury_flower_gu",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The flying bear of Northern Plains is a desolate beast with battle strength that could match Gu Immortals.",
      "chapters": [
        593
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "gu-immortal-match",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside Eighty-Eight True Yang Building, Fang Yuan sees Reckless Savage Demon Venerable facing the immemorial desolate beast Primordial Ash Owl. The text calls immemorial desolate beasts overlords that have existed within heaven and earth since the immemorial era, with rank eight Gu Immortal battle strength. Reckless Savage later eats that rank eight desolate beast as casually as an insufficient meal.",
      "chapters": [
        597
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immemorial-rank-eight",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
        "char_reckless_savage_demon_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Each astral wind flying heavenly boar is an ancient desolate beast that has rank seven Gu Immortal battle strength. Such beasts are rare in the five regions, yet hundreds appear in black heaven. Gu Immortals note that desolate beasts have low intelligence compared with humans. Nearby dark venomous snakes are desolate beast level, while their king snake is an ancient desolate beast.",
      "chapters": [
        1241
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ancient-desolate-rank-seven",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Immemorial desolate beasts have rank eight battle strength, but they are still classified into different tiers. The myriad head coiling dragon is one of the weaker immemorial desolate beasts. Ordinary immemorial desolate beasts cannot deal with Gu Immortals that have rank eight battle strength, because humans have intelligence and can use countless immortal killer moves.",
      "chapters": [
        1467
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tiers-within-immemorial",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Year beasts that use the same desolate-to-immemorial strength ladder are covered on year beast.",
